Architecture Dependencies by Release

Release 1 Dependencies

The successful delivery of Release 1 depends primarily on:
	1.	GCP runtime and platform provisioning
GKE, GCS, BigQuery, and associated cloud platform services must be available and approved.
	2.	Group AI / UDI integration readiness
UDI shared services and AI platform onboarding must be confirmed.
	3.	Workbench integration readiness
UI and backend changes must be aligned to support the production processing flow.
	4.	Security and identity integration
Authentication and authorisation for users and application services must align with enterprise standards.

⸻

Release 2 Dependencies

Release 2 introduces additional strategic dependencies including:
	1.	Neo4j Enterprise platform provisioning
	2.	Enterprise vector store selection and onboarding
	3.	LangGraph runtime and state management design
	4.	MCP gateway deployment and governance
	5.	Ontology governance and versioning
	6.	Metadata / lineage platform readiness
	7.	Event contracts and workflow event model definition

⸻

Overall Summary

The CTB architecture is now intentionally structured as a two-phase platform evolution:
	•	Release 1 productionises the core reauthoring and validation capability on GCP using a simplified application and processing architecture.
	•	Release 2 introduces the full target-state platform architecture required for knowledge graph generation, vector embeddings, governed integration, and future AI-driven knowledge services.

This phased architecture ensures the programme can deliver immediate business value while preserving a clear path to the broader CTB knowledge platform vision.
